{"parentUuid":"9c3b58db-2be2-4661-b3c2-576609e2327b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgarpZAWTQdcW3UhaJExN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":843,"cache_read_input_tokens":915586,"output_tokens":2291,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1260},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":843,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2291,"cache_read_input_tokens":915586,"cache_creation_input_tokens":843,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":843},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":13583,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"4a7945b2-a001-41dc-945e-24d7968a95b4","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgarpYRqr81xGxNGq16i5","requestRef":"2e2a0e22-2510-4f09-aae2-3193a419bb3d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"83b297b1-f57c-4752-9f47-41550b83b41a","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:23:01.810Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"master","slug":"noble-squishing-dawn"}
{"parentUuid":"83b297b1-f57c-4752-9f47-41550b83b41a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgarpZAWTQdcW3UhaJExN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the answer to your question first, then tabs.\n\n**Does each best result apply to the other parts of tuning?** Partly, by design:\n\n| Stage | Shared or per task | What it does |\n|---|---|---|\n| Device (CPU/GPU) | Shared | Chosen once per model; every later stage runs on it. |\n| Quality (context size, KV cache) | Shared | Chosen once per model, measured on a *mix* of all four tasks' questions. |\n| Speed (threads, batch…) | Shared | Chosen once per model, on top of the above. |\n| Sampling and prompt | **Per task** | Chat, code, math and long context each get their own, built on the shared settings above. |\n\nThe shared part is why one preset serves all chats without reloading the model. The cost is that the KV-cache choice is a compromise across tasks. If, say, a lighter cache hurt long context but not code, the mixed measurement could pick it anyway.\n\n**On separating the testing more, which is ModelDuck's differentiator:** I'd **not** split the *presets* further, because fewer questions per preset makes the statistics weak again. I'd make the tests more *visible and separable*:\n\n1. **Show results per question type inside each task.** For example, Code becomes \"write a function / fix a bug / work in a codebase\", and Chat becomes \"follow a format / facts / truthfulness\". A setting that helps one type and hurts another would then be visible, including on the held-back questions.\n2. **Let quality settings be judged per task.** Measure the KV cache per task and keep the shared choice only if no task gets significantly worse; otherwise warn, and say which task loses.\n3. **A \"Benchmark\" tab** describing the test suite itself: each task, its question types, how many questions, how they're checked, and how many are held back. That makes the differentiator visible in the app, not just the README.\n\nTell me which of 1–3 you want. Meanwhile I'll build the tabs.\n\n**The tabs I'm adding:**\n- **Tune:** what to run, the live panel and Continue.\n- **Models:** the model table and the best model per task.\n- **Runs:** tune runs and statistics.\n- **Settings:** the values each setting is tried at.\n- **Benchmark gate:** the old reports.\n\nThe last tab used is remembered, the dialog switches to **Tune** when a tune starts, and the Tune tab shows a dot while one runs. Reading the current dialog structure:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":843,"cache_read_input_tokens":915586,"output_tokens":2291,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1260},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":843,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2291,"cache_read_input_tokens":915586,"cache_creation_input_tokens":843,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":843},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"4a7945b2-a001-41dc-945e-24d7968a95b4","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgarpYRqr81xGxNGq16i5","requestRef":"2e2a0e22-2510-4f09-aae2-3193a419bb3d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7af52b21-4ae5-4072-b391-d3efa996c877","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:23:09.760Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"master","slug":"noble-squishing-dawn"}
