{"parentUuid":"f0ed1bbc-6675-4940-86f0-58d99dd9f83f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgas4tQ2Z7n72a52p41r3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1445,"cache_read_input_tokens":937145,"output_tokens":726,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":22},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1445,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":726,"cache_read_input_tokens":937145,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1445,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1445},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":5973,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"76ce9f6c-8565-41a7-b645-1dbca30ce055","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgas4sxVQeXaXYFzyXYpn","requestRef":"0b8da905-5bf6-4741-b20e-069e578e5694","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a2755a39-7d3a-4af5-b435-186c6aca05cf","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:26:08.319Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"master","slug":"noble-squishing-dawn"}
{"parentUuid":"a2755a39-7d3a-4af5-b435-186c6aca05cf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgas4tQ2Z7n72a52p41r3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The tabs are in and pushed. The Tune & benchmark dialog now has five tabs:\n\n| Tab | What's in it |\n|---|---|\n| **Tune** | What to run, Run all, the live panel and Continue. It shows a dot while a tune runs. |\n| **Models** | The model table and the best model per task. |\n| **Runs** | Every tune run and its statistics; it loads when you open it. |\n| **Tune settings** | The values each setting is tried at, and the CPU/GPU lanes. |\n| **Benchmark gate** | The full benchmark run and older reports. |\n\nThe dialog reopens on the tab you used last, and starting a tune switches to Tune. No tab is longer than about two screens; the whole dialog used to be about nine. I checked each tab in the browser.\n\n**Your question: does each best result apply to the other parts of tuning?**\n- **Device, quality and speed are shared by every task** of a model, and each builds on the previous one.\n- **Sampling and prompt are per task** (chat, code, math, long context), built on top of those shared settings.\n- **The catch:** the KV cache is chosen on a *mix* of all tasks. If a lighter cache hurt long context but not code, the shared choice could still pick it.\n\n**On separating the testing more, which is what makes ModelDuck different.** I wouldn't split the presets into more tasks, because that thins the statistics again. Instead:\n1. **Results per question type within each task**, including on the held-back questions. For example, Code split into write / fix / codebase, and Chat into format / facts / truthfulness, so you can see which kind of question a setting helps or hurts.\n2. **Check the shared quality settings per task.** Keep the shared KV-cache choice only if no task gets significantly worse, and name the task that loses if one does.\n3. **A Benchmark tab** that explains the test suite in the app: each task's question types, counts, how they're checked, and what's held back.\n\nMy suggestion is all three, in that order. Which ones should I build?\n\nThe **one-model baseline** (Coder, one pass) is still running. After it finishes I'll do the real end-to-end live check, commit the baseline and push."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1445,"cache_read_input_tokens":937145,"output_tokens":726,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":22},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1445,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":726,"cache_read_input_tokens":937145,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1445,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1445},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"76ce9f6c-8565-41a7-b645-1dbca30ce055","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgas4sxVQeXaXYFzyXYpn","requestRef":"0b8da905-5bf6-4741-b20e-069e578e5694","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c9268cad-42ad-47b1-a731-e6c3e9a66cd6","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:26:08.528Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"master","slug":"noble-squishing-dawn"}
