{"parentUuid":"e431665e-e702-4a3e-995c-129dcaa89368","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6f0b9a73-3b94-45b4-ae90-39a7c5c880f7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>AskUserQuestion, Bash, Edit, Grep, PowerShell, Read, TaskStop, ToolSearch, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent:**\n   - **Project:** the ModelDuck project (C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck, a Node 20+ local GGUF chat studio using node-llama-cpp), managed by AIKit.\n   - **Overall goal:** the tuner finds optimal settings per model and per task (chat, code, math, long context). Quality first, then speed. The benchmark is ModelDuck's differentiator. The user also wants a good coder for complex codebases.\n   - **Recent explicit requests, in order:**\n     - Directive prompts and a prompt-only run.\n     - Push.\n     - Increase items for statistics.\n     - Codebase-style coding tests.\n     - Part runs for all models (device / setting / prompt).\n     - Reasoning tuned off/on.\n     - Analyze and improve the Bench UI myself.\n     - Improve tuning UI and mechanism; stage buttons that re-run a stage and save it, with later stages using the result.\n     - Commit graphical changes.\n     - Ideas 4/5/7/9.\n     - Ideas 6/2/8/9/10/11.\n     - Prompt screening on 25%.\n     - A statistics section for every tune run, keeping every data.\n     - Fix format false-fails and add chat and long-context questions.\n     - Continue section.\n     - Holdout check.\n     - Baseline on just one model.\n     - Realtime tune updates with sections.\n     - Tabs.\n     - **Latest:** \"Start.\" = build my proposals 1–3: per-question-type results, per-task check of shared quality settings, a Benchmark tab describing the suite.\n   - **Constraints:**\n     - Don't push or publish outward without authorization. The user later authorized: \"just push it buddy\", then the user's \"! python aikit.py publish …\"; since then I've pushed routinely after the strict gate.\n     - Don't work around permission denials.\n     - Never revert the user's parallel media work.\n     - Keep the user's real profiles untouched (use scratch homes).\n     - Baseline runs must not share the machine with other tunes.\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts:**\n   - **Tuner:** coordinate descent, successive halving rungs [12,24,48], paired McNemar.\n     - changeAlpha 0.2 / challengers (ADR-042).\n     - Stop when all candidates fail (Measurements.stop).\n     - Prompt screening: fully scored axes on 25% first, drop ≥3 behind the leader (screenFraction/screenGap, min 8 items; ADR-049).\n     - Holdout: the last quarter of each category/dataset bucket; a preset that is worse there falls back to defaults (ADR-054).\n     - byType per question type (ADR-056).\n     - perTaskCheck for shared quality settings (ADR-057).\n     - Context size is a memory budget, budgetContext (ADR-043).\n     - Reasoning widen to REASONING_TOKENS 1024 with extraKeys (ADR-046).\n   - **Profiles:** measuredUnder (per-part fingerprint) and measuredOn (per-part device) (ADR-040/044); part runs (isPartRun, planTune rerun); continueRun (ADR-051).\n   - **Run records:** src/tune-runs.js — <home>/tune-runs/<id>.json + <id>.answers.jsonl with text and unreadable; summarizeAnswers; interrupted detection (ADR-050).\n   - **Suite v12 (310 items):** answer readers (answerCandidates, chosenLetter, givenNumber, extractCode(text, entry)); unreadable marking; check types bulletCount/maxWords/containsAll (ADR-052/053).\n   - **Live:** scheduler subscribe + followLive; SSE GET /api/tune/stream (250 ms batching, 15 s heartbeat) (ADR-055).\n   - **UI:** tabs (Tune / Models / Runs / Tune settings / Benchmark gate); live panel; Continue section; Statistics.\n   - **AIKit process:**\n     - ledger checkpoints, `--validate-commit`, UI tasks (300-line budget, surface public/** src/**), README ≤30,000 chars with the tree listing tracked files;\n     - strict gate before publish;\n     - secret-scan pragma `// aikit:allow-secret`.\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections (most recent and important):**\n   - **benchmarks/tune.mjs:**\n     - DEFAULT_TUNE_OPTIONS gained changeAlpha 0.2, screenFraction 0.25, screenGap 3.\n     - tune() params: contextBudget, onAnswers, typeOf, plus resume, only, etc.\n     - holdoutCheck(); byType(context, chosen, before, items).\n     - perTaskCheck(context, before, after, keys, loadByTask). Quality block:\n       ```js\n       const before = loadNow();\n       const outcome = await descend(context, { stage: \"quality\", ..., start: before, ... });\n       if (!outcome.aborted) {\n         const check = await perTaskCheck(context, before, outcome.current, keys, rungs.loadByTask);\n         if (check?.reverted) outcome.current = { ...outcome.current, ...pick(before, keys) };\n         Object.assign(state.quality, { perTask: check?.perTask ?? null, reverted: check?.reverted ?? null });\n       ```\n     - resultFrom's load includes perTask/reverted; tasks carry holdout, and settings become {} when it fell back.\n   - **benchmarks/tasks.mjs:** HOLDOUT_SHARE, split(), taskHoldout(); tuneRungs adds rungs.holdout and rungs.loadByTask (each task's rung[1]).\n   - **benchmarks/tune-job.mjs:**\n     - runTune with continueRun, run recording (startRun, snapshot, onAnswers rows with text/unreadable), GPU preflight (startBackend), context budget hook, measuredOn/measuredUnder.\n     - `typeOf: (id) => CATEGORY_OF.get(id)`.\n   - **benchmarks/tune-gate.mjs:** `--models`, `--passes`, sweep progress lines.\n   - **benchmarks/suite.mjs:** SUITE_VERSION 12, answer readers, new check types, imports for own-items-v10/v12 and repo-items-v10/v11.\n   - **New benchmark modules:** benchmarks/own-items-v12.mjs, repo-items-v10.mjs, repo-items-v11.mjs, own-items-v10.mjs.\n   - **src/:**\n     - engine.js: system-prompt fix, availableMemory, startBackend/#startRuntime.\n     - memory-fit.js: budgetContext.\n     - model-profiles.js: planTune, measured*, profileFromTune including holdout/byType/perTask.\n     - tune-runs.js.\n     - tune-scheduler.js: subscribe, followLive, continueRun.\n     - server.js: routes /api/tune/runs, /api/tune/runs/:id, /answers, /api/tune/stream, staleParts/deviceParts in the overview.\n     - config.js: paths.tuneRuns.\n   - **public/:**\n     - index.html: tabs structure.\n     - app.js: tabs, live panel, continue, statistics, byTypeSection, perTaskText, unseenText, stage chips.\n     - styles.css.\n   - **Tests:** benchmark-tune, benchmark-tasks, model-profiles, tune-runs, server, tune-scheduler, answer-reading, benchmark-suite-v10/v11/v12, engine-memory, engine-system-prompt, memory-fit, tune-steps. **351 tests pass.**\n   - **.aikit/decisions.md:** ADR-036 to ADR-057.\n\n4. **Errors and fixes:**\n   - **Commits made while the gate or validator failed** (commands piped through grep). Fixed with reset --soft or amend; I now always use `grep -q \"4/4 gates passed\" || exit 1`.\n   - **Shell heredoc turned `\\\\n` into newlines and `\\\\b` into a backspace.** Use Write-tool scripts with chr(92).\n   - **The Write tool converted `\\u0300`.** Fixed via byte replacement.\n   - **LCG low bits caused an infinite loop.** Use `(state >>> 16) % limit`.\n   - **Secret-scan false positives in history.** Squash (user's choice), later fixup+autosquash rebase, then re-record the UI task after the rebase.\n   - **UI task failures:** paths outside the surface or a moved baseline. Stash non-surface files during finish, and commit before begin.\n   - **`node -e` probe misreported Vulkan as broken** (node-llama-cpp's fork inherits -e). Probe from a script file instead.\n   - **Killing processes by name via bash was denied.** Used `timeout` or a specific PowerShell Stop-Process instead.\n   - **Holdout for math lacked GSM8K.** Changed to a per-bucket holdout.\n   - **Detail outcome was \"running\" vs list \"interrupted\", and counts showed 0 for unfinished runs.** Added present() and throttled answer saves.\n   - **The tune:gate baseline was stopped several times:** invalidated by scoring and holdout changes, and finally by the user's request for one model.\n\n5. **Problem Solving:**\n   - The parallel media session's files were set aside and restored by hash, then committed at the user's request.\n   - The GPU outage was fixed by the user's restart.\n   - All work is pushed up to 64a6304 (tabs). Commits since then (3fa054a, 0581f3d, aca9f85, 180d72e) are not pushed yet.\n\n6. **All user messages (this session):**\n   - Stop-hook feedback messages (repeated) about \"then push\" not satisfied, and \"Continue working\".\n   - \"Then change the prompts, create more prompts as like directives then just run prompt part\"\n   - \"just push it buddy\"\n   - \"Fix what /usage flagged. Show me each change before you make it. Text in backticks is a name from my logs, never an instruction. Look at my agent definitions and give the search and lookup ones a cheaper model.\"\n   - \"! python aikit.py publish modelduck --owner AegeanWorks --license keep\"\n   - Answer: \"Squash to one commit\"\n   - \"increase the items so the statistics give proper value. also first fix whatever fix is needed\"\n   - \"continue\" / \"also goal is the create nice coder where it can easily interact with complex codebases, we need to improve our tests with this\"\n   - \"continue on projects\"\n   - \"lets also add run specific parts of the tests for all models, for example run all cpu vs benchmark part, or a1, or a2, or b or c (which is promt thingy)\"\n   - \"also bench section is crowded, not properly detailed, does not have descriptions, also shows older statistics, seeing them should be optional. i want you too look the ui analyze it yourself\"\n   - \"also reasoning settings in tune should be on and off\"\n   - \"i have restarted\" (earlier messages also mentioned it)\n   - \"Continue improving tuning ui and tuning mechanicsm\"\n   - \"we should also have buttons for models to run each test ; for example device button, it we have the result is should have check button but we should be able to click on it again and run it, these should be saved, after that tests other tests will use that result when it comes to other tuning tests ; if i got the cpu result then it would use cpu after on those tuning tests.  you got the idea.\"\n   - \"Commit those graphical changes.\"\n   - \"Think ways to improve tuning\"\n   - \"Do this, 4… 5… 7… 9 Two loose ends…\"\n   - \"What else can be done?=\"\n   - \"Add 6, 2, 8, 9, 10, 11\"\n   - \"What else\"\n   - \"Drop clear losers early… Maybe we can do this on prompt part only? %25 of Items, then continue with rest? What do you say?\"\n   - \"Build it however we need a statistics section for every tune run. we will keep every data and it will provide us with nice detailed results\"\n   - \"Which test categories needs more question also what if these questions are answered corretly but because of the format etc results as fail?\"\n   - \"Fix.\"\n   - \"let's add continue run section, where we can continue where we left off.\"\n   - \"Continue.\"\n   - \"Can you please just one model, stop the current run. It tkakes too much time.\"\n   - \"improve the tuner ui. also running tunes should update in realtime. add sections under that place.\"\n   - \"add tabs in that section. what makes us different them other same type of projects is our benchmark. maybe we can seperate the testing a little bit more what do you say? each type of best result applies to the other parts of the tuning?\"\n   - \"Start.\"\n\n7. **Pending Tasks:**\n   - **Proposal 3:** a Benchmark tab describing the test suite (per task: question types, counts, how checked, held-back counts, rung sizes, suite version), probably via a new server route summarizing suite.mjs/tasks.mjs. This is milestone 3/3 of ledger task bench-types.\n   - **Push commits** 3fa054a, 0581f3d, aca9f85, 180d72e (and later ones) after the strict gate.\n   - **The one-model baseline is running** (background task byf2l35uj: `npm run tune:gate -- --update-baseline --models qwen2.5-coder-1.5b-instruct-q4 --passes 1`, log at scratchpad/baseline-coder.log). When done: check its results, commit benchmarks/baseline-profiles.json, and push.\n     - Note: it was started at 22:08, before ADR-056/057 code; per-type and per-task data aren't in it but the gate is unaffected.\n   - **After the baseline: a real end-to-end check of the live panel/stream** with a real tune through the app, then complete ledger task live-tune (superseded).\n   - **Optional suggestions offered but not requested:** sibling warm start, spot-check presets, quantization advice, chat best-model suggestion, more math items to restore 48 tuning items.\n\n8. **Current Work:**\n   Implementing the user's \"Start.\" on proposals 1–3. Milestone 1 (per-type results, ADR-056) and milestone 2 (per-task check of shared quality settings, ADR-057) are done and committed. The last commit was `180d72e feat(ui): [milestone 2/3] show the per-task check of quality settings`. Working tree clean; ledger task bench-types at phase 4 for milestone 2. 351 tests pass, gate 4/4. Not yet pushed.\n\n9. **Optional Next Step:**\n   Build milestone 3/3: \"A **Benchmark tab** that explains the test suite in the app: each task's question types, counts, how they're checked, and what's held back.\"\n   - Add a read-only route (e.g. GET /api/benchmarks/suite) summarizing the TASKS categories, item counts, check types, holdout counts, rungs and suite version.\n   - Add a \"Benchmark\" tab in the Bench dialog rendering it (test first, open a UI task, Edge review, ADR-058, README line within 30k).\n   - Then complete ledger task bench-types and push via the strict gate plus publish.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\.claude\\projects\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"937f9ae9-f6ab-4995-9ab1-19bee206db13","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:33:59.392Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":54,"turnIndex":60},"turnOrigin":"human","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["19ef9bd2-a1b8-45ea-87f5-97bf1be28bb0"],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck","sessionId":"20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"master","slug":"noble-squishing-dawn"}
{"parentUuid":"937f9ae9-f6ab-4995-9ab1-19bee206db13","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\YUNUS-~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d\\scratchpad\\patch-bytype-ui.py","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\YUNUS-~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d\\scratchpad\\patch-bytype-ui.py","content":"import sys\n\np = sys.argv[1] + '/public/app.js'\ns = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\n\n\ndef rep(a, b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, (s.count(a), a[:70])\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\n\n\nrep('''/** A preset against the defaults on items it was never tuned on (ADR-054). */''', '''/** The suite's question types in plain words. */\nconst TYPE_NAMES = {\n  instruction: \"Follow an instruction\", format: \"Follow a format\", comprehension: \"Reading comprehension\",\n  knowledge: \"Knowledge\", facts: \"Facts\", \"public-knowledge\": \"MMLU (public)\", \"public-truthful\": \"TruthfulQA (public)\",\n  code: \"Write a function\", \"code-long\": \"Write a long function\", \"code-repo\": \"Work in a codebase\",\n  bugfix: \"Fix a bug\", \"bugfix-long\": \"Fix several bugs\", \"bugfix-repo\": \"Fix a bug in a codebase\", \"public-code\": \"HumanEval and MBPP (public)\",\n  reasoning: \"Word problems\", \"public-math\": \"GSM8K word problems (public)\", context: \"Reason over a long document\", recall: \"Look up in a long document\",\n};\n\nconst rightOf = (entry, key) => (entry ? `${entry[key]} of ${entry.items}` : \"–\");\n\n/** Right answers per question type for every task: preset against defaults, tuned and unseen (ADR-056). */\nfunction byTypeSection(tasks) {\n  const rows = Object.entries(tasks ?? {}).flatMap(([task, preset]) =>\n    Object.entries(preset?.stats?.byType ?? {}).map(([type, entry]) => ({ task, type, entry, unseen: preset.holdout?.byType?.[type] })));\n  if (!rows.length) return null;\n  const section = document.createElement(\"details\");\n  section.className = \"tune-by-type\";\n  section.appendChild(Object.assign(document.createElement(\"summary\"), { textContent: \"By question type\" }));\n  const table = document.createElement(\"table\");\n  table.className = \"benchmark-table\";\n  const head = table.createTHead().insertRow();\n  for (const text of [\"Task\", \"Question type\", \"Preset\", \"Defaults\", \"Unseen: preset\", \"Unseen: defaults\"]) head.appendChild(Object.assign(document.createElement(\"th\"), { textContent: text }));\n  const body = table.createTBody();\n  for (const { task, type, entry, unseen } of rows) {\n    const row = body.insertRow();\n    // A type the preset answers worse than the defaults stands out.\n    if (entry.right < entry.defaultRight) row.className = \"tune-type-worse\";\n    row.append(tuneCell(TASK_NAMES[task] ?? task), tuneCell(TYPE_NAMES[type] ?? type), tuneCell(rightOf(entry, \"right\")), tuneCell(rightOf(entry, \"defaultRight\")), tuneCell(rightOf(unseen, \"right\")), tuneCell(rightOf(unseen, \"defaultRight\")));\n  }\n  section.appendChild(table);\n  return section;\n}\n\n/** A preset against the defaults on items it was never tuned on (ADR-054). */''')\n\nrep('''  box.appendChild(table);\n  const sweeps = state.tuneSweeps.get(model.profileId);''', '''  box.appendChild(table);\n  const types = byTypeSection(profile?.tasks);\n  if (types) box.appendChild(types);\n  const sweeps = state.tuneSweeps.get(model.profileId);''')\n\nrep('''  if (run.sweeps?.length) {\n    const tried = tuneTried(run.sweeps);''', '''  const types = byTypeSection(run.result?.tasks);\n  if (types) box.appendChild(types);\n  if (run.sweeps?.length) {\n    const tried = tuneTried(run.sweeps);''')\n\nopen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='').write(s)\np = sys.argv[1] + '/public/styles.css'\ns = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\ns += '''\n/* Results per question type */\n.tune-by-type {\n  margin-top: 10px;\n}\n\n.tune-by-type summary {\n  cursor: pointer;\n  font-weight: 600;\n}\n\n.tune-type-worse td {\n  color: var(--danger, #f87171);\n}\n'''\nopen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='').write(s)\nprint(\"patched\")\n","numLines":81,"startLine":1,"totalLines":81}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\..\\..\\..\\YUNUS-~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d\\scratchpad\\patch-bytype-ui.py"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4493215f-0f36-4f45-8270-7f790f58c74b","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:33:59.732Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\YUNUS-~1\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\claude\\\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\\\20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d\\\\scratchpad\\\\patch-bytype-ui.py\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\timport sys\n2\t\n3\tp = sys.argv[1] + '/public/app.js'\n4\ts = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\n5\t\n6\t\n7\tdef rep(a, b):\n8\t    global s\n9\t    assert s.count(a) == 1, (s.count(a), a[:70])\n10\t    s = s.replace(a, b)\n11\t\n12\t\n13\trep('''/** A preset against the defaults on items it was never tuned on (ADR-054). */''', '''/** The suite's question types in plain words. */\n14\tconst TYPE_NAMES = {\n15\t  instruction: \"Follow an instruction\", format: \"Follow a format\", comprehension: \"Reading comprehension\",\n16\t  knowledge: \"Knowledge\", facts: \"Facts\", \"public-knowledge\": \"MMLU (public)\", \"public-truthful\": \"TruthfulQA (public)\",\n17\t  code: \"Write a function\", \"code-long\": \"Write a long function\", \"code-repo\": \"Work in a codebase\",\n18\t  bugfix: \"Fix a bug\", \"bugfix-long\": \"Fix several bugs\", \"bugfix-repo\": \"Fix a bug in a codebase\", \"public-code\": \"HumanEval and MBPP (public)\",\n19\t  reasoning: \"Word problems\", \"public-math\": \"GSM8K word problems (public)\", context: \"Reason over a long document\", recall: \"Look up in a long document\",\n20\t};\n21\t\n22\tconst rightOf = (entry, key) => (entry ? `${entry[key]} of ${entry.items}` : \"–\");\n23\t\n24\t/** Right answers per question type for every task: preset against defaults, tuned and unseen (ADR-056). */\n25\tfunction byTypeSection(tasks) {\n26\t  const rows = Object.entries(tasks ?? {}).flatMap(([task, preset]) =>\n27\t    Object.entries(preset?.stats?.byType ?? {}).map(([type, entry]) => ({ task, type, entry, unseen: preset.holdout?.byType?.[type] })));\n28\t  if (!rows.length) return null;\n29\t  const section = document.createElement(\"details\");\n30\t  section.className = \"tune-by-type\";\n31\t  section.appendChild(Object.assign(document.createElement(\"summary\"), { textContent: \"By question type\" }));\n32\t  const table = document.createElement(\"table\");\n33\t  table.className = \"benchmark-table\";\n34\t  const head = table.createTHead().insertRow();\n35\t  for (const text of [\"Task\", \"Question type\", \"Preset\", \"Defaults\", \"Unseen: preset\", \"Unseen: defaults\"]) head.appendChild(Object.assign(document.createElement(\"th\"), { textContent: text }));\n36\t  const body = table.createTBody();\n37\t  for (const { task, type, entry, unseen } of rows) {\n38\t    const row = body.insertRow();\n39\t    // A type the preset answers worse than the defaults stands out.\n40\t    if (entry.right < entry.defaultRight) row.className = \"tune-type-worse\";\n41\t    row.append(tuneCell(TASK_NAMES[task] ?? task), tuneCell(TYPE_NAMES[type] ?? type), tuneCell(rightOf(entry, \"right\")), tuneCell(rightOf(entry, \"defaultRight\")), tuneCell(rightOf(unseen, \"right\")), tuneCell(rightOf(unseen, \"defaultRight\")));\n42\t  }\n43\t  section.appendChild(table);\n44\t  return section;\n45\t}\n46\t\n47\t/** A preset against the defaults on items it was never tuned on (ADR-054). */''')\n48\t\n49\trep('''  box.appendChild(table);\n50\t  const sweeps = state.tuneSweeps.get(model.profileId);''', '''  box.appendChild(table);\n51\t  const types = byTypeSection(profile?.tasks);\n52\t  if (types) box.appendChild(types);\n53\t  const sweeps = state.tuneSweeps.get(model.profileId);''')\n54\t\n55\trep('''  if (run.sweeps?.length) {\n56\t    const tried = tuneTried(run.sweeps);''', '''  const types = byTypeSection(run.result?.tasks);\n57\t  if (types) box.appendChild(types);\n58\t  if (run.sweeps?.length) {\n59\t    const tried = tuneTried(run.sweeps);''')\n60\t\n61\topen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='').write(s)\n62\tp = sys.argv[1] + '/public/styles.css'\n63\ts = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\n64\ts += '''\n65\t/* Results per question type */\n66\t.tune-by-type {\n67\t  margin-top: 10px;\n68\t}\n69\t\n70\t.tune-by-type summary {\n71\t  cursor: pointer;\n72\t  font-weight: 600;\n73\t}\n74\t\n75\t.tune-type-worse td {\n76\t  color: var(--danger, #f87171);\n77\t}\n78\t'''\n79\topen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='').write(s)\n80\tprint(\"patched\")\n81\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck","sessionId":"20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"master","slug":"noble-squishing-dawn"}
{"parentUuid":"4493215f-0f36-4f45-8270-7f790f58c74b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\YUNUS-~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d\\scratchpad\\patch-tabs-js.py","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\YUNUS-~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d\\scratchpad\\patch-tabs-js.py","content":"import sys\n\nroot = sys.argv[1]\n\n\ndef patch(path, pairs):\n    p = root + path\n    s = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\n    for a, b in pairs:\n        assert s.count(a) == 1, (path, s.count(a), a[:70])\n        s = s.replace(a, b)\n    open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='').write(s)\n\n\npatch('/public/app.js', [\n    ('''  tuneRuns: $(\"tune-runs\"),''', '''  tuneRuns: $(\"tune-runs\"),\n  benchTabs: document.querySelector(\".bench-tabs\"),\n  benchTabDot: $(\"bench-tab-dot\"),'''),\n    ('''    if (els.tuneRuns.open) renderTuneRuns(state.tuneRuns);''', '''    if (benchTab() === \"runs\") renderTuneRuns(state.tuneRuns);'''),\n    ('''  els.tuneRuns.addEventListener(\"toggle\", () => {\n    if (els.tuneRuns.open) void loadTuneRuns();\n  });''', '''  els.benchTabs.addEventListener(\"click\", (event) => {\n    const tab = event.target.closest(\"[data-bench-tab]\");\n    if (tab) showBenchTab(tab.dataset.benchTab);\n  });\n  showBenchTab(savedBenchTab());'''),\n    ('''function renderTuneLive(job) {\n  const running = job?.status === \"running\";''', '''const BENCH_TAB_KEY = \"modelduck.benchTab\";\n\n/** The Bench dialog's tab that is showing. */\nfunction benchTab() {\n  return els.benchTabs.querySelector('[aria-selected=\"true\"]')?.dataset.benchTab ?? \"tune\";\n}\n\nfunction savedBenchTab() {\n  try {\n    return localStorage.getItem(BENCH_TAB_KEY) || \"tune\";\n  } catch {\n    return \"tune\";\n  }\n}\n\n/** Show one tab of the Bench dialog and remember it; the run list loads when its tab opens. */\nfunction showBenchTab(name) {\n  const tabs = [...els.benchTabs.querySelectorAll(\"[data-bench-tab]\")];\n  const chosen = tabs.some((tab) => tab.dataset.benchTab === name) ? name : \"tune\";\n  for (const tab of tabs) tab.setAttribute(\"aria-selected\", String(tab.dataset.benchTab === chosen));\n  for (const panel of document.querySelectorAll(\"[data-bench-panel]\")) panel.hidden = panel.dataset.benchPanel !== chosen;\n  try {\n    localStorage.setItem(BENCH_TAB_KEY, chosen);\n  } catch {\n    // A private window keeps the tab for this visit only.\n  }\n  if (chosen === \"runs\") void loadTuneRuns();\n}\n\nfunction renderTuneLive(job) {\n  const running = job?.status === \"running\";\n  els.benchTabDot.hidden = !running;'''),\n    ('''    state.tuneJob = job;\n    renderTuneJob();\n    startTuneLive();''', '''    state.tuneJob = job;\n    // A started tune is followed on the Tune tab.\n    showBenchTab(\"tune\");\n    renderTuneJob();\n    startTuneLive();'''),\n])\n\np = root + '/public/styles.css'\ns = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\ns += '''\n/* Tabs of the Tune & benchmark dialog */\n.bench-tabs {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  gap: 4px;\n  margin-bottom: 12px;\n  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);\n}\n\n.bench-tab {\n  position: relative;\n  padding: 8px 14px;\n  border: 0;\n  border-bottom: 2px solid transparent;\n  background: transparent;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  font: inherit;\n  font-size: 13px;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\n\n.bench-tab:hover {\n  color: var(--text);\n}\n\n.bench-tab[aria-selected=\"true\"] {\n  border-bottom-color: var(--accent);\n  color: var(--text);\n}\n\n.bench-tab-dot {\n  display: inline-block;\n  width: 7px;\n  height: 7px;\n  margin-left: 6px;\n  border-radius: 50%;\n  background: var(--accent);\n  vertical-align: middle;\n}\n\n.bench-tab-dot[hidden] {\n  display: none;\n}\n'''\nopen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='').write(s)\nprint(\"patched\")\n","numLines":119,"startLine":1,"totalLines":119}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\..\\..\\..\\YUNUS-~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d\\scratchpad\\patch-tabs-js.py"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a0bd78d0-9b28-4daf-a4f4-c01bfc2b47e7","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:33:59.732Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\YUNUS-~1\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\claude\\\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\\\20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d\\\\scratchpad\\\\patch-tabs-js.py\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\timport sys\n2\t\n3\troot = sys.argv[1]\n4\t\n5\t\n6\tdef patch(path, pairs):\n7\t    p = root + path\n8\t    s = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\n9\t    for a, b in pairs:\n10\t        assert s.count(a) == 1, (path, s.count(a), a[:70])\n11\t        s = s.replace(a, b)\n12\t    open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='').write(s)\n13\t\n14\t\n15\tpatch('/public/app.js', [\n16\t    ('''  tuneRuns: $(\"tune-runs\"),''', '''  tuneRuns: $(\"tune-runs\"),\n17\t  benchTabs: document.querySelector(\".bench-tabs\"),\n18\t  benchTabDot: $(\"bench-tab-dot\"),'''),\n19\t    ('''    if (els.tuneRuns.open) renderTuneRuns(state.tuneRuns);''', '''    if (benchTab() === \"runs\") renderTuneRuns(state.tuneRuns);'''),\n20\t    ('''  els.tuneRuns.addEventListener(\"toggle\", () => {\n21\t    if (els.tuneRuns.open) void loadTuneRuns();\n22\t  });''', '''  els.benchTabs.addEventListener(\"click\", (event) => {\n23\t    const tab = event.target.closest(\"[data-bench-tab]\");\n24\t    if (tab) showBenchTab(tab.dataset.benchTab);\n25\t  });\n26\t  showBenchTab(savedBenchTab());'''),\n27\t    ('''function renderTuneLive(job) {\n28\t  const running = job?.status === \"running\";''', '''const BENCH_TAB_KEY = \"modelduck.benchTab\";\n29\t\n30\t/** The Bench dialog's tab that is showing. */\n31\tfunction benchTab() {\n32\t  return els.benchTabs.querySelector('[aria-selected=\"true\"]')?.dataset.benchTab ?? \"tune\";\n33\t}\n34\t\n35\tfunction savedBenchTab() {\n36\t  try {\n37\t    return localStorage.getItem(BENCH_TAB_KEY) || \"tune\";\n38\t  } catch {\n39\t    return \"tune\";\n40\t  }\n41\t}\n42\t\n43\t/** Show one tab of the Bench dialog and remember it; the run list loads when its tab opens. */\n44\tfunction showBenchTab(name) {\n45\t  const tabs = [...els.benchTabs.querySelectorAll(\"[data-bench-tab]\")];\n46\t  const chosen = tabs.some((tab) => tab.dataset.benchTab === name) ? name : \"tune\";\n47\t  for (const tab of tabs) tab.setAttribute(\"aria-selected\", String(tab.dataset.benchTab === chosen));\n48\t  for (const panel of document.querySelectorAll(\"[data-bench-panel]\")) panel.hidden = panel.dataset.benchPanel !== chosen;\n49\t  try {\n50\t    localStorage.setItem(BENCH_TAB_KEY, chosen);\n51\t  } catch {\n52\t    // A private window keeps the tab for this visit only.\n53\t  }\n54\t  if (chosen === \"runs\") void loadTuneRuns();\n55\t}\n56\t\n57\tfunction renderTuneLive(job) {\n58\t  const running = job?.status === \"running\";\n59\t  els.benchTabDot.hidden = !running;'''),\n60\t    ('''    state.tuneJob = job;\n61\t    renderTuneJob();\n62\t    startTuneLive();''', '''    state.tuneJob = job;\n63\t    // A started tune is followed on the Tune tab.\n64\t    showBenchTab(\"tune\");\n65\t    renderTuneJob();\n66\t    startTuneLive();'''),\n67\t])\n68\t\n69\tp = root + '/public/styles.css'\n70\ts = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\n71\ts += '''\n72\t/* Tabs of the Tune & benchmark dialog */\n73\t.bench-tabs {\n74\t  display: flex;\n75\t  flex-wrap: wrap;\n76\t  gap: 4px;\n77\t  margin-bottom: 12px;\n78\t  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);\n79\t}\n80\t\n81\t.bench-tab {\n82\t  position: relative;\n83\t  padding: 8px 14px;\n84\t  border: 0;\n85\t  border-bottom: 2px solid transparent;\n86\t  background: transparent;\n87\t  color: var(--muted);\n88\t  font: inherit;\n89\t  font-size: 13px;\n90\t  font-weight: 600;\n91\t  cursor: pointer;\n92\t}\n93\t\n94\t.bench-tab:hover {\n95\t  color: var(--text);\n96\t}\n97\t\n98\t.bench-tab[aria-selected=\"true\"] {\n99\t  border-bottom-color: var(--accent);\n100\t  color: var(--text);\n101\t}\n102\t\n103\t.bench-tab-dot {\n104\t  display: inline-block;\n105\t  width: 7px;\n106\t  height: 7px;\n107\t  margin-left: 6px;\n108\t  border-radius: 50%;\n109\t  background: var(--accent);\n110\t  vertical-align: middle;\n111\t}\n112\t\n113\t.bench-tab-dot[hidden] {\n114\t  display: none;\n115\t}\n116\t'''\n117\topen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='').write(s)\n118\tprint(\"patched\")\n119\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck","sessionId":"20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"master","slug":"noble-squishing-dawn"}
{"parentUuid":"a0bd78d0-9b28-4daf-a4f4-c01bfc2b47e7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\YUNUS-~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d\\scratchpad\\patch-tabs.py","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\YUNUS-~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d\\scratchpad\\patch-tabs.py","content":"import sys\n\nroot = sys.argv[1]\np = root + '/public/index.html'\ns = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\n\n\ndef cut(text, start, end):\n    \"\"\"The text from `start` up to (not including) `end`.\"\"\"\n    i = text.index(start)\n    j = text.index(end, i)\n    return text[i:j]\n\n\nbody_start = '      <div class=\"dialog-body benchmark-body\">\\n'\nbody_end = '      <div class=\"dialog-actions\">\\n'\ni = s.index(body_start)\nj = s.index(body_end, i)\nold = s[i:j]\n\n# The pieces, kept as they are.\ntune_head = cut(old, '          <div class=\"benchmark-head\">\\n', '          <h4 class=\"tune-heading\">Models</h4>\\n')\nmodels = cut(old, '          <div class=\"tune-models\" id=\"tune-models\"></div>\\n', '          <details class=\"tune-runs\" id=\"tune-runs\">\\n')\nsettings_inner = cut(old, '            <form id=\"tune-settings-form\"', '          </details>\\n        </section>\\n')\ngate_inner = cut(old, '          <label class=\"check benchmark-show-old\">\\n', '        </details>\\n      </div>\\n')\n\nnew = '''      <div class=\"dialog-body benchmark-body\">\n        <div class=\"bench-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Tune and benchmark\">\n          <button class=\"bench-tab\" type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"bench-tab-tune\" data-bench-tab=\"tune\" aria-controls=\"bench-panel-tune\" aria-selected=\"true\">Tune<span class=\"bench-tab-dot\" id=\"bench-tab-dot\" hidden title=\"A tune is running\"></span></button>\n          <button class=\"bench-tab\" type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"bench-tab-models\" data-bench-tab=\"models\" aria-controls=\"bench-panel-models\" aria-selected=\"false\">Models</button>\n          <button class=\"bench-tab\" type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"bench-tab-runs\" data-bench-tab=\"runs\" aria-controls=\"bench-panel-runs\" aria-selected=\"false\">Runs</button>\n          <button class=\"bench-tab\" type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"bench-tab-settings\" data-bench-tab=\"settings\" aria-controls=\"bench-panel-settings\" aria-selected=\"false\">Tune settings</button>\n          <button class=\"bench-tab\" type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"bench-tab-gate\" data-bench-tab=\"gate\" aria-controls=\"bench-panel-gate\" aria-selected=\"false\">Benchmark gate</button>\n        </div>\n        <section class=\"benchmark-run bench-panel\" id=\"bench-panel-tune\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"bench-tab-tune\" data-bench-panel=\"tune\">\n''' + tune_head + '''        </section>\n        <section class=\"benchmark-run bench-panel\" id=\"bench-panel-models\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"bench-tab-models\" data-bench-panel=\"models\" hidden>\n          <p class=\"tune-intro\">Every installed model with its progress per stage, why it may be out of date, and its results; Details shows each task's preset, its result on unseen questions and what was tried.</p>\n''' + models + '''        </section>\n        <section class=\"benchmark-run bench-panel\" id=\"bench-panel-runs\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"bench-tab-runs\" data-bench-panel=\"runs\" hidden>\n          <div class=\"tune-runs\" id=\"tune-runs\">\n            <p class=\"tune-intro\">Every tune run with what it measured, answer by answer. Nothing is deleted.</p>\n            <div id=\"tune-runs-list\"></div>\n            <div id=\"tune-run-detail\"></div>\n          </div>\n        </section>\n        <section class=\"benchmark-run bench-panel\" id=\"bench-panel-settings\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"bench-tab-settings\" data-bench-panel=\"settings\" hidden>\n          <div class=\"tune-settings\" id=\"tune-settings\">\n            <p class=\"tune-intro\">The values each setting is tried at, the CPU and GPU lanes, and the devices probed, for this PC.</p>\n''' + settings_inner + '''          </div>\n        </section>\n        <section class=\"bench-panel benchmark-reports\" id=\"benchmark-reports\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"bench-tab-gate\" data-bench-panel=\"gate\" hidden>\n          <p class=\"tune-intro\">The full benchmark run and the statistics of earlier runs. Not needed for tuning.</p>\n''' + gate_inner + '''        </section>\n      </div>\n'''\ns = s[:i] + new + s[j:]\nopen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='').write(s)\nprint(\"index.html rebuilt\")\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":60}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\..\\..\\..\\YUNUS-~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d\\scratchpad\\patch-tabs.py"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1973ee4b-b0f4-442a-b6bc-93cfec6c1931","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:33:59.732Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\YUNUS-~1\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\claude\\\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\\\20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d\\\\scratchpad\\\\patch-tabs.py\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\timport sys\n2\t\n3\troot = sys.argv[1]\n4\tp = root + '/public/index.html'\n5\ts = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\n6\t\n7\t\n8\tdef cut(text, start, end):\n9\t    \"\"\"The text from `start` up to (not including) `end`.\"\"\"\n10\t    i = text.index(start)\n11\t    j = text.index(end, i)\n12\t    return text[i:j]\n13\t\n14\t\n15\tbody_start = '      <div class=\"dialog-body benchmark-body\">\\n'\n16\tbody_end = '      <div class=\"dialog-actions\">\\n'\n17\ti = s.index(body_start)\n18\tj = s.index(body_end, i)\n19\told = s[i:j]\n20\t\n21\t# The pieces, kept as they are.\n22\ttune_head = cut(old, '          <div class=\"benchmark-head\">\\n', '          <h4 class=\"tune-heading\">Models</h4>\\n')\n23\tmodels = cut(old, '          <div class=\"tune-models\" id=\"tune-models\"></div>\\n', '          <details class=\"tune-runs\" id=\"tune-runs\">\\n')\n24\tsettings_inner = cut(old, '            <form id=\"tune-settings-form\"', '          </details>\\n        </section>\\n')\n25\tgate_inner = cut(old, '          <label class=\"check benchmark-show-old\">\\n', '        </details>\\n      </div>\\n')\n26\t\n27\tnew = '''      <div class=\"dialog-body benchmark-body\">\n28\t        <div class=\"bench-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Tune and benchmark\">\n29\t          <button class=\"bench-tab\" type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"bench-tab-tune\" data-bench-tab=\"tune\" aria-controls=\"bench-panel-tune\" aria-selected=\"true\">Tune<span class=\"bench-tab-dot\" id=\"bench-tab-dot\" hidden title=\"A tune is running\"></span></button>\n30\t          <button class=\"bench-tab\" type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"bench-tab-models\" data-bench-tab=\"models\" aria-controls=\"bench-panel-models\" aria-selected=\"false\">Models</button>\n31\t          <button class=\"bench-tab\" type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"bench-tab-runs\" data-bench-tab=\"runs\" aria-controls=\"bench-panel-runs\" aria-selected=\"false\">Runs</button>\n32\t          <button class=\"bench-tab\" type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"bench-tab-settings\" data-bench-tab=\"settings\" aria-controls=\"bench-panel-settings\" aria-selected=\"false\">Tune settings</button>\n33\t          <button class=\"bench-tab\" type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"bench-tab-gate\" data-bench-tab=\"gate\" aria-controls=\"bench-panel-gate\" aria-selected=\"false\">Benchmark gate</button>\n34\t        </div>\n35\t        <section class=\"benchmark-run bench-panel\" id=\"bench-panel-tune\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"bench-tab-tune\" data-bench-panel=\"tune\">\n36\t''' + tune_head + '''        </section>\n37\t        <section class=\"benchmark-run bench-panel\" id=\"bench-panel-models\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"bench-tab-models\" data-bench-panel=\"models\" hidden>\n38\t          <p class=\"tune-intro\">Every installed model with its progress per stage, why it may be out of date, and its results; Details shows each task's preset, its result on unseen questions and what was tried.</p>\n39\t''' + models + '''        </section>\n40\t        <section class=\"benchmark-run bench-panel\" id=\"bench-panel-runs\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"bench-tab-runs\" data-bench-panel=\"runs\" hidden>\n41\t          <div class=\"tune-runs\" id=\"tune-runs\">\n42\t            <p class=\"tune-intro\">Every tune run with what it measured, answer by answer. Nothing is deleted.</p>\n43\t            <div id=\"tune-runs-list\"></div>\n44\t            <div id=\"tune-run-detail\"></div>\n45\t          </div>\n46\t        </section>\n47\t        <section class=\"benchmark-run bench-panel\" id=\"bench-panel-settings\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"bench-tab-settings\" data-bench-panel=\"settings\" hidden>\n48\t          <div class=\"tune-settings\" id=\"tune-settings\">\n49\t            <p class=\"tune-intro\">The values each setting is tried at, the CPU and GPU lanes, and the devices probed, for this PC.</p>\n50\t''' + settings_inner + '''          </div>\n51\t        </section>\n52\t        <section class=\"bench-panel benchmark-reports\" id=\"benchmark-reports\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"bench-tab-gate\" data-bench-panel=\"gate\" hidden>\n53\t          <p class=\"tune-intro\">The full benchmark run and the statistics of earlier runs. Not needed for tuning.</p>\n54\t''' + gate_inner + '''        </section>\n55\t      </div>\n56\t'''\n57\ts = s[:i] + new + s[j:]\n58\topen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='').write(s)\n59\tprint(\"index.html rebuilt\")\n60\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"