:"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck","sessionId":"20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"master","slug":"noble-squishing-dawn"}
{"parentUuid":"26de88ea-9f24-4f2a-b2d2-17b1418193d1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6f0b9a73-3b94-45b4-ae90-39a7c5c880f7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S6peNv3NzFhuUhh38n8aLT","type":"tool_result","content":"                                  --desc DESC [--why WHY]\n  --task TASK           task ID\n  --phase-num {1,2,3,4,5}\n  --desc DESC           what was done; a plan starts '[1/M]'\n  --why WHY             impact assessment, required on a task's first plan\n  --benefits BENEFITS   impact assessment, required on a task's first plan\n  --risks RISKS         impact assessment, required on a task's first plan\n  --mitigation MITIGATION\n  --handoff HANDOFF     cold-start packet: 'next: ...' plus optional state,\n  --redact              record credential-shaped text as [REDACTED] instead of\nProject:   modelduck  (C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck)\r\nRepo:      https://github.com/AegeanWorks/Modelduck.git\r\nStacks:    node\r\nLicense:   personal (AL-1.1, free personal use)\r\nTests:     npm test\r\nDecision:  ADR-057: The shared quality settings are checked on every task\r\nGuidelines: 5 rule(s) in .aikit/guidelines.md; they add to and rank below AIKit's principles (PRINCIPLE-000 R6).\r\n  - **G-001** (user, ADR-027): Every change that can affect generation, prompt construction, settings application or the chat UI must run `npm run tune:gate` on the three core models and compare each task's quality and speed with that model's stored profile baseline; a task-rate drop beyond the tune tolerance is a regression. Cross-model comparison (`npm run bench:compare`) is optional and never gates.\r\n  - **G-002** (user): Every benchmark run is stored in benchmarks/history.sqlite and appended to benchmarks/history.jsonl; after committing the benchmarked change, run npm run bench:link to attach the run to its commit, and keep the JSONL history tracked.\r\n  - **G-003** (user, ADR-027): Tune results are comparable only when suiteVersion, the task-subset hash and the runtime match; any prompt, check, task subset or sweep change bumps SUITE_VERSION, updates benchmarks/CHANGELOG.md and requires a deliberate profile-baseline update. The optional cross-model baseline may lag the suite version.\r\n  - **G-004** (user): Presets are benchmark candidates: they fill the settings form only and are never applied automatically until a benchmark run has recorded their quality and speed.\r\n  - **G-005** (user, ADR-027): A tune has two stages: model-load settings first (one load config per model, chosen for speed and memory without losing quality), then sampling settings per task on that config; both stages must be recorded before a profile is applied.\r\n============================================================\r\n⚡ DISRUPTION RESUMPTION GUIDANCE (PRINCIPLE-006)\r\n============================================================","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"fef81c78-ff8f-45d4-a168-0aeedcf1a377","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:35:02.677Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"                                  --desc DESC [--why WHY]\n  --task TASK           task ID\n  --phase-num {1,2,3,4,5}\n  --desc DESC           what was done; a plan starts '[1/M]'\n  --why WHY             impact assessment, required on a task's first plan\n  --benefits BENEFITS   impact assessment, required on a task's first plan\n  --risks RISKS         impact assessment, required on a task's first plan\n  --mitigation MITIGATION\n  --handoff HANDOFF     cold-start packet: 'next: ...' plus optional state,\n  --redact              record credential-shaped text as [REDACTED] instead of\nProject:   modelduck  (C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck)\r\nRepo:      https://github.com/AegeanWorks/Modelduck.git\r\nStacks:    node\r\nLicense:   personal (AL-1.1, free personal use)\r\nTests:     npm test\r\nDecision:  ADR-057: The shared quality settings are checked on every task\r\nGuidelines: 5 rule(s) in .aikit/guidelines.md; they add to and rank below AIKit's principles (PRINCIPLE-000 R6).\r\n  - **G-001** (user, ADR-027): Every change that can affect generation, prompt construction, settings application or the chat UI must run `npm run tune:gate` on the three core models and compare each task's quality and speed with that model's stored profile baseline; a task-rate drop beyond the tune tolerance is a regression. Cross-model comparison (`npm run bench:compare`) is optional and never gates.\r\n  - **G-002** (user): Every benchmark run is stored in benchmarks/history.sqlite and appended to benchmarks/history.jsonl; after committing the benchmarked change, run npm run bench:link to attach the run to its commit, and keep the JSONL history tracked.\r\n  - **G-003** (user, ADR-027): Tune results are comparable only when suiteVersion, the task-subset hash and the runtime match; any prompt, check, task subset or sweep change bumps SUITE_VERSION, updates benchmarks/CHANGELOG.md and requires a deliberate profile-baseline update. The optional cross-model baseline may lag the suite version.\r\n  - **G-004** (user): Presets are benchmark candidates: they fill the settings form only and are never applied automatically until a benchmark run has recorded their quality and speed.\r\n  - **G-005** (user, ADR-027): A tune has two stages: model-load settings first (one load config per model, chosen for speed and memory without losing quality), then sampling settings per task on that config; both stages must be recorded before a profile is applied.\r\n============================================================\r\n⚡ DISRUPTION RESUMPTION GUIDANCE (PRINCIPLE-006)\r\n============================================================","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"4755b055-bb9c-409d-81b1-0f41f1bdaccb","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/modelduck","