{"parentUuid":"9c0cd9d8-894f-4198-af63-701d857b997c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgaskobury8goistpcPjk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VNbLwhFnuEyC8HmnnLNg1s","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/modelduck && cat >> .aikit/decisions.md <<'EOF'\n\n### ADR-058: The app describes the benchmark suite\n- **Date**: 2026-11-01\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: The suite is what sets ModelDuck apart, but what it asks was only visible in the source: which question types each task has, how many items, where they come from, how answers are checked and how many are held back.\n- **Decision**: `suiteSummary()` in `benchmarks/tasks.mjs` derives, per task, the items, the held-back items, the items tuned on and the rung sizes, and per question type the items, held-back items, sources (own or the public dataset) and check types, from the suite itself. `GET /api/benchmarks/suite` returns it, and a Benchmark tab in the Tune and benchmark dialog shows it in plain words.\n- **Consequences**: The description cannot drift from the suite, since it is computed from the same items and split the tuner uses.\nEOF\ntimeout 60 python ../../aikit.py check modelduck 2>&1 | tail -4","description":"Record ADR-058 and run the project gates","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1197,"cache_read_input_tokens":75844,"output_tokens":549,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":55},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1197,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":549,"cache_read_input_tokens":75844,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1197,"cache_creat