{"parentUuid":"98b2b11b-9023-4381-8e11-c0591d6f63e0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgatFGwzwJPihmXjfUVCi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":216,"cache_read_input_tokens":105210,"output_tokens":690,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":22},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":216,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":690,"cache_read_input_tokens":105210,"cache_creation_input_tokens":216,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":216},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":5816,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"595921a9-5ac2-4f8c-8937-ccf702eefa61","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgatFGUyETagGJtKAr5Aa","requestRef":"84e7931f-3d0b-45ac-8986-af78da75706c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"094cdb31-4838-41b1-aa53-6855c95ce7e9","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:41:35.891Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck","sessionId":"20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"master","slug":"noble-squishing-dawn"}
{"parentUuid":"094cdb31-4838-41b1-aa53-6855c95ce7e9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgatFGwzwJPihmXjfUVCi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've built all three proposals, and they're pushed (`64a6304..c8eaa77`). All 353 tests pass and the strict gate passed 4/4.\n\n1. **Results by question type.** Each task's result is now split by question type, for example \"Work in a codebase\", \"Fix a bug\" and \"GSM8K word problems\". It shows the preset next to the defaults, both on the questions it was tuned on and on held-back questions. A type where the preset does worse than the defaults is marked. You'll find it in a model's Details and in each run's detail. Most types have fewer than 15 questions, so these numbers show where to look rather than prove a difference.\n2. **Shared settings checked on every task.** Context size and KV cache are shared by all of a model's tasks. After choosing them, the tuner now checks each task on its own. If any task gets clearly worse, it goes back to the settings it had before. Details shows each task's result and which task caused the switch back. This reuses answers already measured, so it costs no extra time.\n3. **New Benchmark tab** in the Tune & benchmark dialog. It describes the whole suite: version 12, 310 questions across Chat (84), Code (112), Math (51) and Long context (63). For each question type it shows how many questions there are, how many are held back, where they come from (ModelDuck's own, HumanEval, MBPP, GSM8K, MMLU or TruthfulQA) and how answers are checked, such as \"code that passes its tests\" or \"chosen letter\". It's built from the same questions and split the tuner uses, so it can't drift out of date. I checked it in headless Edge: no console errors, and the dialog reopens on the tab you last had open.\n\nThe one-model baseline for `qwen2.5-coder-1.5b-instruct-q4` is still running and has reached the Code sampling stage. It started before the first two changes, so its saved profile won't include the per-type and per-task numbers. That doesn't affect the gate. When it finishes, I'll check its results, then commit and push `benchmarks/baseline-profiles.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":216,"cache_read_input_tokens":105210,"output_tokens":690,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":22},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":216,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":690,"cache_read_input_tokens":105210,"cache_creation_input_tokens":216,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":216},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"595921a9-5ac2-4f8c-8937-ccf702eefa61","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgatFGUyETagGJtKAr5Aa","requestRef":"84e7931f-3d0b-45ac-8986-af78da75706c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3ca0e585-4869-40fe-b871-cacfac632cab","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:41:35.897Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck","sessionId":"20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"master","slug":"noble-squishing-dawn"}
