{"parentUuid":"27b32916-dcd1-4ad6-a455-5ab6c48edef5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgatHANfYkEBVUq6kRJ5j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's what I'd do next, most useful first.\n\n**For quality and your coding goal**\n1. **Add questions to the thin types.** The Benchmark tab makes the gaps plain: Knowledge has 3 questions, and Fix several bugs, Fix a bug in a codebase and Write a long function have 6 each. Math tunes on 38 questions, not 48. With so few, the per-type results can only hint at a difference. I'd bring each type to at least 12, starting with the codebase ones.\n2. **Harder codebase tests.** Today's codebase questions are one prompt, one answer. For \"a coder that handles complex codebases\", I'd add questions spread over several files, a fix that starts from a stack trace or failing test output, and an edit to an existing file that is checked by running its tests. This tests what you actually want the model to do.\n3. **Show \"too few to tell\" on per-type rows.** Mark a type whose difference is within noise, so a red row on 4 questions isn't read as a real loss.\n\n**For tune time**\n4. **Re-check instead of re-tune.** When the runtime, driver or suite changes, first re-score the saved preset on the held-back questions (a few minutes). Only run a full re-tune if it got worse.\n5. **Start from a sibling model's result.** A new quant of an already-tuned model would start from that model's preset, which should cut most of the tuning rounds.\n\n**For users of the app**\n6. **Suggest a model per task in chat.** For example: \"for code, Qwen2.5-Coder 1.5B scored best\". The best-model table already holds this; the chat task picker just doesn't use it.\n7. **Quantization advice.** Compare q4 and q8 of the same model per question type, and say whether the bigger file is worth the memory.\n\n**Still open from before:** once the baseline finishes, I'll run a real tune through the app to confirm the live view works end to end.\n\nI'd start with 1 and 2, because they make every other result more trustworthy and match your coding goal. Should I go ahead with those?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":700,"cache_read_input_tokens":105426,"output_tokens":1174,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":516},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":700,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1174,"cache_read_input_tokens":105426,"cache_creation_input_tokens":700,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":700},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e6ff4e46-c60f-4e25-a758-fa363116b243","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgatH9xMne48GfSDCdZ3z","requestRef":"0a59bfbd-5490-4a02-a9f5-62246b328fbb","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"bb7c9cdd-a61f-4c2b-9818-fa20decfef8b","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:42:08.674Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck","sessionId":"20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"master","slug":"noble-squishing-dawn"}
