{"parentUuid":"bcd1d1c3-837c-4597-985c-da4a23c5321d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgatyywzWAC9WNRcfh3zp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0118Lu71os3jD4rZ7vjfsAxm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> .aikit/decisions.md <<'EOF'\n\n### ADR-059: Per-type results say when they are too few to tell\n- **Date**: 2026-11-01\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: ADR-056 shows right answers per question type, but most types have under 15 items, so a row where the preset is two answers behind the defaults was marked as worse even when that is within noise.\n- **Decision**: Each `byType` entry carries `p`, the exact McNemar test of that type's own paired answers (items the defaults got right and the preset lost, against the reverse). Details and a run's detail add a column: \"clearly better\" or \"clearly worse\" when p < 0.05, otherwise \"too few to tell\"; only a clearly worse type is marked.\n- **Consequences**: Profiles tuned before this have no `p`; their rows show \"–\" and keep the old marking. The task-level paired test stays the decision rule.\nEOF\ntimeout 500 npm test 2>&1 | grep -E \"^ℹ (pass|fail)\"; cd ../.. && python aikit.py checkpoint modelduck --agent claude-opus-5.5 --task suite-v13 --phase-num 4 --desc \"[1/3] byType entries carry each type's paired p (ADR-059); the column follows in the UI task. checklists: passed\" 2>&1 | tail -1; cd projects/modelduck && git add benchmarks/tune.mjs tests/benchmark-tune.test.js .aikit/decisions.md .aikit/task_ledger.json && { timeout 400 python ../../aikit.py check modelduck 2>&1 | grep -q \"4/4 gates passed\" || { echo GATE FAIL; exit 1; }; } && git commit -q -m \"feat(tune): test each question type's difference on its own\n\nEach byType entry carries the exact paired p of that type's answers, so a\nper-type difference too small to tell apart can say so (ADR-059).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git log --oneline -1 && git status --short","description":"Test, gate and commit the per-type p","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":933,"cache_read_input_tokens":124986,"output_tokens":1129,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":273},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":933,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1129,"cache_read_input_tokens":124986,"cache_creation_input_tokens":933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":933},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0118Lu71os3jD4rZ7vjfsAxm":{"command":"cd /c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/modelduck && cat >> .aikit/decisions.md <<'EOF'\n\n### ADR-059: Per-type results say when they are too few to tell\n- **Date**: 2026-11-01\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: ADR-056 shows right answers per question type, but most types have under 15 items, so a row where the preset is two answers behind the defaults was marked as worse even when that is within noise.\n- **Decision**: Each `byType` entry carries `p`, the exact McNemar test of that type's own paired answers (items the defaults got right and the preset lost, against the reverse). Details and a run's detail add a column: \"clearly better\" or \"clearly worse\" when p < 0.05, otherwise \"too few to tell\"; only a clearly worse type is marked.\n- **Consequences**: Profiles tuned before this have no `p`; their rows show \"–\" and keep the old marking. The task-level paired test stays the decision rule.\nEOF\ntimeout 500 npm test 2>&1 | grep -E \"^ℹ (pass|fail)\"; cd ../.. && python aikit.py checkpoint modelduck --agent claude-opus-5.5 --task suite-v13 --phase-num 4 --desc \"[1/3] byType entries carry each type's paired p (ADR-059); the column follows in the UI task. checklists: passed\" 2>&1 | tail -1; cd projects/modelduck && git add benchmarks/tune.mjs tests/benchmark-tune.test.js .aikit/decisions.md .aikit/task_ledger.json && { timeout 400 python ../../aikit.py check modelduck 2>&1 | grep -q \"4/4 gates passed\" || { echo GATE FAIL; exit 1; }; } && git commit -q -m \"feat(tune): test each question type's difference on its own\n\nEach byType entry carries the exact paired p of that type's answers, so a\nper-type difference too small to tell apart can say so (ADR-059).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git log --oneline -1 && git status --short","description":"Test, gate and commit the per-type p","timeout":600000}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_0118Lu71os3jD4rZ7vjfsAxm":{"cwd":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/modelduck"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"cc8dc072-70f9-473f-b089-29a988039ddc","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgatyyibsscoptEmnw9rF","requestRef":"e305753b-a634-4dfe-91f7-e10d112cb600","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"be66e570-0ad3-4908-92d7-f45d3c757072","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:51:18.339Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck","sessionId":"20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"master","slug":"noble-squishing-dawn"}
