he source: which question types each task has, how many items, where they come from, how answers are checked and how many are held back."," - **Decision**: `suiteSummary()` in `benchmarks/tasks.mjs` derives, per task, the items, the held-back items, the items tuned on and the rung sizes, and per question type the items, held-back items, sources (own or the public dataset) and check types, from the suite itself. `GET /api/benchmarks/suite` returns it, and a Benchmark tab in the Tune and benchmark dialog shows it in plain words."," - **Consequences**: The description cannot drift from the suite, since it is computed from the same items and split the tuner uses.","+","+### ADR-059: Per-type results say when they are too few to tell","+- **Date**: 2026-11-01","+- **Status**: Accepted","+- **Context**: ADR-056 shows right answers per question type, but most types have under 15 items, so a row where the preset is two answers behind the defaults was marked as worse even when that is within noise.","+- **Decision**: Each `byType` entry carries `p`, the exact McNemar test of that type's own paired answers (items the defaults got right and the preset lost, against the reverse). Details and a run's detail add a column: \"clearly better\" or \"clearly worse\" when p < 0.05, otherwise \"too few to tell\"; only a clearly worse type is marked.","+- **Consequences**: Profiles tuned before this have no `p`; their rows show \"–\" and keep the old marking. The task-level paired test stays the decision rule."]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck\\.aikit\\task_ledger.json","hunks":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":31,"newStart":2,"newLines":15,"lines":["   \"version\": 1,\r","   \"active_task\": {\r","     \"task_id\": \"suite-v13\",\r","-    \"last_phase\": \"phase 2\",\r","-    \"active_phase\": 2,\r","+    \"last_phase\": \"phase 4\",\r","+    \"active_phase\": 4,\r","     \"status\": \"in_progress\",\r","-    \"updated_at\": 1793476239.133