r\",\n      \"evaluates an arithmetic expression string made of non-negative integers, +, -, *, / and parentheses, with any spaces. \" +\n      \"Use the usual precedence (* and / before + and -), evaluate operators of equal precedence left to right, and use ordinary division, so 10 / 4 is 2.5. \" +\n      \"Do not use eval or the Function constructor; parse the expression yourself.\",\n      \"evaluate\", [c([\"2 + 3 * 4\"], 14), c([\"(2 + 3) * 4\"], 20), c([\"10 / 4\"], 2.5), c([\"8 - 3 - 2\"], 3), c([\"2 * (3 + (4 - 1)) / 3\"], 4)], { long: true }),\n    code(\"code-long-csv\", \"Parse a CSV line\",\n      \"parses one line of CSV into an array of field strings. Fields are separated by commas. A field may be wrapped in double quotes; inside quotes a comma is part of the field and two double quotes in a row stand for one double quote. \" +\n      \"An empty line is one empty field, and empty fields between commas are kept.\",\n      \"parseCsvLine\", [c([\"a,b,c\"], [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]), c(['\"x, y\",z'], [\"x, y\", \"z\"]), c(['\"he said \"\"hi\"\"\",ok'], ['he said \"hi\"', \"ok\"]), c([\"\"], [\"\"]), c([\"a,,b\"], [\"a\", \"\", \"b\"])], { long: true }),\n    code(\"code-long-word-wrap\", \"Greedy word wrap\",\n      \"wraps text into lines of at most width characters and returns the lines as an array. Words are separated by whitespace and joined by single spaces; \" +\n      \"fill each line greedily with as many words as fit, and put a word longer than width on a line of its own. Empty text gives an empty array.\",\n      \"wrapText\", [c([\"the quick brown fox jumps\", 10], [\"the quick\", \"brown fox\", \"jumps\"]), c([\"hello\", 3], [\"hello\"]), c([\"a b c d\", 3], [\"a b\", \"c d\"]), c([\"\", 5], [])], { long: true }),\n    code(\"code-long-checkout\", \"Shop checkout with offers\",\n      \"computes a shop total. Its arguments are cart, an array of { item, qty }; prices, an object mapping item names to unit prices; and discounts, an object mapping item names to a number N meaning \\\"buy N, get one free\\\" \" +\n      \"(in every complete group of N + 1 units of that item, one unit is free). Items without a price are ignored. Return the total rounded to cents as a number.\",\n      \"checkout\", [\n        c([[{ item: \"apple\", qty: 3 }], { apple: 0.5 }, {}], 1.5),\n        c([[{ item: \"apple\", qty: 3 }], { apple: 0.5 }, { apple: 2 }], 1),\n        c([[{ item: \"apple\", qty: 7 }, { item: \"pear\", qty: 2 }], { apple: 0.5, pear: 1.25 }, { apple: 2 }], 5),\n        c([[{ item: \"kiwi\", qty: 2 }], { apple: 1 }, {}], 0),\n      ], { long: true }),\n    code(\"code-long-matrix-multiply\", \"Matrix multiplication\",\n      \"multiplies two matrices given as arrays of rows and returns the product, or null when the number of columns of the first does not equal the number of rows of the second.\",\n      \"multiply\", [c([[[1, 2], [3, 4]], [[5, 6], [7, 8]]], [[19, 22], [43, 50]]), c([[[1, 2, 3]], [[4], [5], [6]]], [[32]]), c([[[1, 2]], [[1, 2]]], null)], { long: true }),\n    code(\"code-long-ini\", \"Parse an INI config\",\n      \"parses INI-style text into an object of sections. A line [name] starts a section; a line key = value adds a key to the current section, with both sides trimmed and the value kept as a string. \" +\n      \"Keys before the first section go into a section named \\\"\\\" (an empty string). Blank lines and lines starting with ; or # are ignored. Text with no keys or sections gives an empty object.\",\n      \"parseIni\", [\n        c([\"a=1\\n[db]\\nhost = localhost\\nport=5432\\n; comment\\n[ui]\\ntheme = dark\"], { \"\": { a: \"1\" }, db: { host: \"localhost\", port: \"5432\" }, ui: { theme: \"dark\" } }),\n        c([\"\"], {}),\n        c([\"# only a comment\\n[x]\\nk=v\"], { x: { k: \"v\" } }),\n      ], { long: true }),\n  ];\n}\n\n93:      \"evaluate\", [c([\"2 + 3 * 4\"], 14), c([\"(2 + 3) * 4\"], 20), c([\"10 / 4\"], 2.5), c([\"8 - 3 - 2\"], 3), c([\"2 * (3 + (4 - 1)) / 3\"], 4)]