able_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck","sessionId":"20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"master","slug":"noble-squishing-dawn"}
{"parentUuid":"fe4a2ed1-ea43-4e38-ac3a-1abcb5e00506","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bcb4eca5-d71f-4719-8be6-c39f68cbc6f4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017HWbFEkprYVJ5J2tS6ujSJ","type":"tool_result","content":"- **AI benchmark gate** - two phases: model reload/quantization/KV-cache settings,\n  then sampling/prompting settings, with test hashes so result changes are not\n  confused with test edits.\n\n## AI benchmark gate\n\nThe required gate is `npm run tune:gate` (ADR-027). This seeded, batch-1\ncross-model benchmark on the real `LlamaEngine` is optional: the **model reload**\nphase (`npm run bench`) changes one load setting at a time across models, and the\n**model usage** phase (`npm run bench:chat`) compares sampling and prompting on a\nchosen configuration.\n\nThree small model classes are the default required set: SmolLM2 135M (tiny), Qwen2.5\n0.5B (general) and Qwen2.5 Coder 1.5B (code). `--full-matrix` / `npm run bench:full`\nadds Qwen2.5 1.5B, Llama 3.2 3B and Phi-3.5 Mini plus their KV-cache variants; that\ndeeper review takes hours on a CPU and is opt-in. Suite v13 runs 344 items: 284\nquestions ModelDuck authored (code, multi-file codebases, bug fixes, chat, math,\nlong context, comprehension, facts) plus 60 items copied from\npermissively licensed public benchmarks (GSM8K 16, MMLU 12,\nHumanEval 12, MBPP 8 and TruthfulQA 12) with source and licence recorded per item;\nsee [benchmarks/NOTICE-benchmarks.md](benchmarks/NOTICE-benchmarks.md). Public items\nmay be in a model's training data, so the report shows **own questions** and\n**public benchmarks** as separate origins, with public results per dataset.\n\n```bash\nnpm run bench -- --download        # first run: fetch missing models, core phase\nnpm run bench:all                  # optional: add the model-usage phase\nnpm run bench:full                 # optional: add Llama 3B and Phi 3.8B\nnpm run bench -- --model <id>      # settings sweep for one model; never touches a baseline\nnpm run bench:update               # deliberately replace both baselines\nnpm run bench:update:model         # deliberately replace only the model baseline\nnpm run bench:update:full          # replace the model baseline with six models\nnpm run bench:report\nnpm run bench:link                 # after commit: attach the run to HEAD\nnpm run verify:manifest -- --models-dir ..\\models\n```\n\n`verify:manifest` is an opt-in real-model check that does not write history or\nchange baselines. It proves session reuse, 40-message truncation, prompt\nrepetition, a completion after a chat session, chat-template identity and runtime\nidentity on an installed GGUF.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3106ca05-e88e-4d9d-ad87-2d94f4c4bb4c","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:01:15.920Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"- **AI benchmark gate** - two phases: model reload/quantization/KV-cache settings,\n  then sampling/prompting settings, with test hashes so result changes are not\n  confused with test edits.\n\n## AI benchmark gate\n\nThe required gate is `npm run tune:gate` (ADR-027). This seeded, batch-1\ncross-model benchmark on the real `LlamaEngine` is optional: the **model reload**\nphase (`npm run bench`) changes one load setting at a time across models, and the\n**model usage** phase (`npm run bench:chat`) compares sampling and prompting on a\nchosen configuration.\n\nThree small model classes are the default required set: SmolLM2 135M (tiny), Qwen2.5\n0.5B (general) and Qwen2.5 Coder 1.5B (code). `--full-matrix` / `npm run bench:full`\nadds Qwen2.5 1.5B, Llama 3.2 3B and Phi-3.5 Mini plus their KV-cache variants; that\ndeeper review takes hours on a CPU and is opt-in. Suite v13 runs 344 items: 284\nquestions ModelDuck authored (code, multi-file codebases, bug fixes, chat, math,\nlong context, comprehension, facts) plus 60 items copied from\npermissively licensed public benchmarks (GSM8K 16, MMLU 12,\nHumanEval 12, MBPP 8 and TruthfulQA 12) with source and licence recorded per item;\nsee [benchmarks/NOTICE-benchmarks.md](benchmarks/NOTICE-benchmarks.md). Public items\nmay be in a model's training data, so the report shows **own questions** and\n**public benchmarks** as separate origins, with public results per dataset.\n\n```bash\nnpm run bench -- --download        # first run: fetch missing models, core phase\nnpm run bench:all                  # optional: add the model-usage phase\nnpm run bench:full                 # optional: add Llama 3B and Phi 3.8B\nnpm run bench -- --model <id>      # settings sweep for one model; never touches a baseline\nnpm run bench:update               # deliberately replace both baselines\nnpm run bench:update:model         # deliberately replace only the model baseline\nnpm run bench:update:full          # replace the model baseline with six models\nnpm run bench:report\nnpm run bench:link                 # after commit: attach the run to HEAD\nnpm run verify:manifest -- --models-dir ..\\models\n```\n\n`verify:manifest` is an opt-in real-model check that does not write history or\nchange baselines. It proves session reuse, 40-message truncation, prompt\nrepetition, a completion after a chat session, chat-template identity and runtime\nidentity on an installed GGUF.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8d76ceda-213e-41df-be8f-8db1f08cd534","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/modelduck","root":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/modelduck","branch":"master","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":6,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":3},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"AegeanWorks/Modelduck","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"AegeanWorks/Modelduck","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"h