e-v11.test.js"," │   ├── benchmark-suite-v12.test.js"," │   ├── benchmark-suite-v13.test.js","+│   ├── benchmark-suite-v13-repo.test.js"," │   ├── reference-solutions-v9.js"," │   ├── reference-solutions-v13.js"," │   ├── benchmark-test-hash.test.js"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck\\benchmarks\\CHANGELOG.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":19,"oldLines":7,"newStart":19,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | v10 | 2026-10-31 | 256 items (was 174): 30 own math word problems, 40 generated recall items and 12 multi-file codebase items (`code-repo`, `bugfix-repo`: write a function on the existing helpers, fix a reported bug, name the function holding a bug). A `jsTests` check can carry `setup`, the codebase loaded before the answer. Math and recall reach 51 items each; tuning rungs grow from 6/12/24 to 12/24/48. Test and task-subset hashes change, so saved tune profiles show a suite-changed warning until re-tuned. |"," | v11 | 2026-10-31 | 268 items (was 256): 12 items on three larger codebases with six or seven files each (a bank ledger, an order and shipping service, a Markdown renderer): six functions to write, three reported bugs to fix, three bugs to locate. The code task grows to 112 items. Test and task-subset hashes change, so saved tune profiles show a suite-changed warning until re-tuned. |"," | v12 | 2026-10-31 | 310 items (was 268): 30 chat items that test following an instruction or a format, checked by new bullet-count, word-limit and contains-all checks, and 12 long-context items (two-step lookups, event order, absence, cross-references). Checkers read answers the way a person would (lead-ins, labels, Markdown, \"Answer: B\", the number after \"Answer\", the code block defining the function) and mark unreadable replies apart from wrong ones, so scores of earlier suites are not comparable. Saved tune profiles show a suite-changed warning until re-tuned. |","-| v13 | 2026-11-01 | 344 items (was 310): 9 knowledge questions, 6 long functions to write and 6 long functions with several bugs bring each of those types to 12, and 13 math word problems bring math to 64 items so it tunes on 48 like chat and code (ADR-060). Reference answers, failing buggy versions and independently worked math answers are in tests. |","+| v13 | 2026-11-01 | 356 items (was 310): 9 knowledge questions, 6 long functions to write and 6 long functions with several bugs bring each of those types to 12, and 13 math word problems bring math to 64 items so it tunes on 48 like chat and code (ADR-060). 12 codebase items: six changes that span several functions or files and six fixes that start from a failing test and its output, checked through a hidden scenario that runs after the reply (ADR-061). Reference answers, failing buggy versions, the quoted outputs and independently worked math answers are proven in tests. |"," | v8 | 2026-10-30 | 130 items (was 91): own questions grow to 70 (instruction, reasoning, knowledge, format, code, bugfix, comprehension, recall, facts and context each gain items) and public items to 60 — GSM8K 16, MMLU 12, TruthfulQA 12, HumanEval 12 and MBPP 8. The number check now reads the **last** number in the reply (GSM8K answers often follow working), and math prompts get 512 tokens and an explicit \"Answer: <number>\" ending so a model is not cut off mid-reasoning. Public items also expose a per-dataset breakdown. Test hash changes; replace the baseline deliberately. |"," "," When adding or changing a prompt, check or matrix variant:"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck\\README.md","C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck\\benchmarks\\CHANGELOG.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b24473ff-40c2-454b-973e-e02547cdd5c7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/modelduck","root":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/modelduc