{"parentUuid":"4f6808f4-88ea-4d11-b1c8-53ab4c1d8f40","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgavA69wgdaWs1Y8dfaKx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GjzA7EmzPqMgBpZtXcayFh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> .aikit/decisions.md <<'EOF'\n\n### ADR-061: Codebase items that span functions or start from a failing test\n- **Date**: 2026-11-01\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: Every codebase item asked for one named function, either a new one, the corrected one or the culprit's name, so a model was never asked to change several functions together or to work back from a failing test to a cause in another file, which is most of real maintenance.\n- **Decision**: `benchmarks/repo-items-v13.mjs` adds a planner codebase (seven files with a distractor) and twelve items on it and the v11 codebases: six changes that need more than one function or file changed (task priorities, the day a task was done, hours per tag, a transfer fee, stacked discount codes, numbered lists) and six fixes given only a failing test and its real output, whose cause lies outside the function the test calls. A `jsTests` check may carry `harness`: the reply's code blocks are all kept, in order, and a hidden `scenario` function defined after them runs the cases, so any function the reply redefines replaces the codebase's own; a reply with no function definition is unreadable. `tests/benchmark-suite-v13-repo.test.js` proves every case passes with a reference reply, fails on the unchanged codebase, that each quoted output is what the shipped codebase really produces, and that a reply split over two code blocks passes in the sandbox.\n- **Consequences**: Suite v13 has 356 items; code has 124, still tuned on 48. Older items keep the single-block reading of ADR-052.\nEOF\ncd ../.. && python aikit.py checkpoint modelduck --agent claude-opus-5.5 --task suite-v13 --phase-num 4 --desc \"[3/3] 12 codebase items: six multi-function changes and six fixes from a failing test's output, checked through a hidden scenario that keeps every code block (ADR-061). checklists: passed\" 2>&1 | tail -1 && cd projects/modelduck && git add benchmarks/repo-items-v13.mjs benchmarks/repo-items-v10.mjs benchmarks/repo-items-v11.mjs benchmarks/suite.mjs benchmarks/CHANGELOG.md tests/benchmark-suite-v13-repo.test.js tests/benchmark-suite-v13.test.js tests/benchmark-suite-v6.test.js README.md .aikit/decisions.md .aikit/task_ledger.json && git status --short | grep -v \"^[AM] \" ; timeout 400 python ../../aikit.py check modelduck 2>&1 | grep -E \"gates passed|FAIL\" | head -5","description":"Record ADR-061, checkpoint, stage and gate","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":446,"cache_read_input_tokens":225644,"output_tokens":1037,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":446,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1037,"cache_read_input_tokens":225644,"cache_creation_input_tokens":446,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":446},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01GjzA7EmzPqMgBpZtXcayFh":{"command":"cd /c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/modelduck && cat >> .aikit/decisions.md <<'EOF'\n\n### ADR-061: Codebase items that span functions or start from a failing test\n- **Date**: 2026-11-01\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: Every codebase item asked for one named function, either a new one, the corrected one or the culprit's name, so a model was never asked to change several functions 