 write (an LRU cache, a query-string parser, a dependency sort, a text table, the next calendar day, a Sudoku check), 6 long functions with more than one bug each, and 13 math word problems. Each long function passes its cases with a reference in `tests/reference-solutions-v13.js`, each buggy function fails at least two of its cases, and each math answer is worked out again independently in `tests/benchmark-suite-v13.test.js`. With 64 math items, the last quarter of each bucket (16) is held back and math tunes on 48."," - **Consequences**: 344 items, suite v13: every saved profile and the tune:gate baseline are stale until re-tuned. The exact suite totals are now pinned by the v13 test; the v12 test checks at least its own total, and the v9 counts are taken over the v9 items only, so no earlier check got looser about what it covers.","+","+### ADR-061: Codebase items that span functions or start from a failing test","+- **Date**: 2026-11-01","+- **Status**: Accepted","+- **Context**: Every codebase item asked for one named function, either a new one, the corrected one or the culprit's name, so a model was never asked to change several functions together or to work back from a failing test to a cause in another file, which is most of real maintenance.","+- **Decision**: `benchmarks/repo-items-v13.mjs` adds a planner codebase (seven files with a distractor) and twelve items on it and the v11 codebases: six changes that need more than one function or file changed (task priorities, the day a task was done, hours per tag, a transfer fee, stacked discount codes, numbered lists) and six fixes given only a failing test and its real output, whose cause lies outside the function the test calls. A `jsTests` check may carry `harness`: the reply's code blocks are all kept, in order, and a hidden `scenario` function defined after them runs the cases, so any function the reply redefines replaces the codebase's own; a reply with no function definition is unreadable. `tests/benchmar