{"parentUuid":"1bd5c2a8-d34b-45c5-b09f-2cd935c27fdc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgavCzfPhkDDKZW2tu5Df","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've built all three, and they're pushed (`c8eaa77..22d4dab`). All 362 tests pass and the strict gate passed 4/4.\n\n1. **\"Too few to tell\" on per-type rows.** Each question type now gets its own statistical test comparing the preset with the defaults on the same questions. The \"By question type\" table has a new Difference column showing \"clearly better\", \"clearly worse\", \"too few to tell\" or \"same\". Only clearly worse rows are marked red. Profiles tuned before this show \"–\" there. I checked it in headless Edge with sample data.\n2. **Thin types filled (suite v13).** I added 9 knowledge questions, 6 long functions to write, 6 long functions with several bugs, and 13 math word problems.\n   - Knowledge, long functions and long bug fixes now have 12 questions each.\n   - Math has 64, so it now tunes on 48 questions like chat and code (it was 38).\n   - Tests confirm every reference answer passes, every buggy version fails, and every math answer matches an independent calculation.\n3. **Harder codebase tests.** There's a new 7-file task-planner codebase, plus 12 items on it and on the existing ones:\n   - **6 changes that touch more than one function or file**, for example task priorities, a transfer fee, stacked discount codes and numbered lists in the Markdown renderer.\n   - **6 fixes that start from a failing test and its output**, as you'd paste it, where the cause is in a different file from where it fails. For example, a \"no account for Ann\" error is raised in `getAccount`, but the cause is in `openAccount`.\n   - The answer may change any functions and use several code blocks. A hidden check runs the result afterwards. Tests confirm each quoted test output is what the broken code really produces.\n\nTo make room for the new questions in the README I trimmed three sentences: the default model list, the full benchmark run's description and the `verify:manifest` description.\n\n**Decision for you:** I stopped the one-model baseline that was running. Adding questions makes every saved profile and the tune:gate baseline out of date, so the old run's result would have been useless. A new baseline needs a re-tune on v13, which takes a few hours for the Coder model alone. Should I start it now?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":290,"cache_read_input_tokens":228296,"output_tokens":779,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":49},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":290,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":779,"cache_read_input_tokens":228296,"cache_creation_input_tokens":290,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":290},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e3400f14-fed2-4447-b0a2-eec07cdaf69a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgavCzN2wDwomdpABm8Yk","requestRef":"5424fe92-8cd4-4d18-8927-7562e6022761","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f80ca91d-a615-44ed-8446-dc727da66be1","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:07:19.816Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck","sessionId":"20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"master","slug":"noble-squishing-dawn"}
