{"parentUuid":"02c5c94c-4b07-4b7b-ae8c-464418697365","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgavF76eSscQh88jrgagq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":793,"cache_read_input_tokens":228586,"output_tokens":1382,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":726},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":793,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1382,"cache_read_input_tokens":228586,"cache_creation_input_tokens":793,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":793},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":8364,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"fe7d9cbc-253c-492d-8512-aaa5ee4e56be","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgavF6dcnFuV1QLeb6trd","requestRef":"715419af-a849-44bf-a821-4778fbb572ae","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"fe99c582-32d5-449a-ba65-136867c76b1e","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:07:49.421Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck","sessionId":"20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"master","slug":"noble-squishing-dawn"}
{"parentUuid":"fe99c582-32d5-449a-ba65-136867c76b1e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgavF76eSscQh88jrgagq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's what I'd change in the tuner, most useful first.\n\n**Save time**\n1. **Reuse answers across runs.** Each run already caches answers within itself. Keeping them across runs would mean a re-tune only answers questions it hasn't seen before. An answer is only reused when the model file, runtime, settings, seed and question are all the same. This matters right now: v13 made every profile stale, but 310 of its 356 questions are unchanged. A re-tune would mostly ask the 46 new ones, so minutes instead of hours.\n2. **Re-check before re-tuning.** When the suite or runtime changes, first score the saved preset on the held-back questions. Only re-tune the parts that got worse.\n3. **Stop a round once it's decided.** If a candidate is so far behind that it couldn't catch up even by winning every remaining question, drop it right away. The result can't change, so this is pure saving.\n4. **Start from a sibling model's result.** A new quant of an already-tuned model would start from that model's settings, so most tuning rounds end quickly.\n\n**Get better results**\n5. **Split a task when its question types disagree.** If a setting is clearly better for one type and clearly worse for another, for example writing functions versus fixing bugs, tune separate presets for each. Until now these differences couldn't be told apart; the new \"clearly better / clearly worse\" check makes them visible.\n6. **Check pairs of settings together.** The tuner changes one setting at a time, so it misses pairs that only help in combination, such as temperature with top-p. After the normal pass, a small check would try the best two values of the two settings that mattered most, together.\n7. **Measure speed on long prompts too.** Speed is measured mostly on short questions. Long-context and codebase use depend on how fast the prompt is read, so the chosen settings could be slow exactly where it matters.\n\nI'd start with 1 and 2. Together they turn the v13 re-tune you just declined, and every future suite change, from hours into minutes. Want me to build those?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":793,"cache_read_input_tokens":228586,"output_tokens":1382,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":726},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":793,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1382,"cache_read_input_tokens":228586,"cache_creation_input_tokens":793,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":793},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"fe7d9cbc-253c-492d-8512-aaa5ee4e56be","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgavF6dcnFuV1QLeb6trd","requestRef":"715419af-a849-44bf-a821-4778fbb572ae","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ddfac415-4d6a-4f29-ac1f-fc7b856642bb","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:07:56.278Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck","sessionId":"20b8d1d8-5397-4bf1-8838-6d05c82b6c1d","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"master","slug":"noble-squishing-dawn"}
